al answer\n\nFrom (1) we already know that no value larger than \\(n\\) can occur.  \nThe inductive construction shows that **every** integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) can be realised.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For a given }n\\ge 3\\text{ the admissible values of }k\\text{ are }0,1,\\dots ,n.}\n\\]"
