n### 4.  Construction for any \\(k\\ge 3\\)\n\nLet \\(k\\) satisfy \\(3\\le k\\le n\\) and put \\(r=n-k\\).  \n\n1. **Non‑sunny part.**  \n   Use the \\(r\\) vertical lines  \n\n   \\[\n   x=1,\\;x=2,\\dots ,x=r .\n   \\]\n\n   They are non‑sunny and distinct.\n\n2. **Remaining points.**  \n   The points of \\(S_n\\) not covered by the above vertical lines are exactly  \n\n   \\[\n   \\{(a,b)\\mid a>r,\\;a+b\\le n+1\\}\n   =\\{(a',b)\\mid a'+b\\le k+1\\}=S_k ,\n   \\]\n\n   where \\(a'=a-r\\).\n\n3. **Sunny part.**  \n   By Lemma 2, \\(S_k\\) can be covered by exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines; none of these lines is vertical, hence they are distinct from the previously used \\(r\\) lines.\n\nAltogether we have \\(r+k=n\\) distinct lines, exactly \\(k\\) of which are sunny, and they cover every point of \\(S_n\\). ∎\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Conclusion\n\nThe admissible numbers of sunny lines are\n\n\\[\nk=0,\\qquad k=1,\\qquad\\text{and all }k\\text{ with }3\\le k\\le n .\n\\]\n\nThe value \\(k=2\\) never occurs.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1\\}\\cup\\{3,4,\\dots ,n\\}\\;}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
