 of \\(n\\) distinct lines with exactly\n\\(k\\) sunny lines covering all points of \\(S_n\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Impossibility of other values\n\nThe definition of \\(k\\) already forces \\(0\\le k\\le n\\); the construction above\nshows that every integer in this interval is attainable.  Hence no other\nvalues of \\(k\\) are possible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Answer**\n\nFor every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the admissible numbers of sunny lines are exactly\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k=0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\; } .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
