int of \\(T_m\\).\n\n   Finally we add the two forced lines \\(x=1\\) and \\(y=1\\).  \n   The total number of lines is  \n\n   \\[\n   2+s+t = 2+s+(m-s)=n,\n   \\]\n\n   and the number of sunny lines is exactly \\(s=k\\).  \n   Thus the required configuration exists.\n\n5. **Conclusion.**  \n   The forced lines give the lower bound \\(k\\ge0\\).  \n   Inequality (1) gives the sharp upper bound.  \n   The inductive construction shows that every integer between the bounds is attainable.  \n   Hence the set of admissible \\(k\\) is exactly the one stated above.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For }n=3:\\;k\\in\\{0,1\\};\\qquad\n\\text{for }n\\ge4:\\;0\\le k\\le\\Big\\lfloor\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Big\\rfloor } .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
